<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pinerolo</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pinerolo is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piedmont">Piedmont</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, south-west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turin">Turin</a> at the entrance to the valleys leading to the French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a>. From the 1290s it was the seat of the Savoy-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaea">Achaea</a> branch that ruled Piedmont. Seized repeatedly by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, it was French from 1631 to 1696, when its fortress held notable prisoners such as Nicolas Fouquet and the Man in the Iron Mask.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pinerolo.jpg" alt="Pinerolo" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Zairon · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pinerolo_Basilica_di_San_Maurizio_Terrazza_4.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
